<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  CRYSTAL_INGEST_EXECUTION_1 item 2 (design/Jawa/mods/crystal_mods_inventory.md ss1/ss3,
  ratified 2026-09-10): "gate its genstep to Lantern Deeps maps" for lee.theforce.
  lightsaber's kyber. Measured two things before touching anything (per the item's own
  "verify which genstep is actually firing" instruction, same discipline as the KOTOR
  discrepancy check):

  1. Force_CrystalFormation_{Small,Medium,Large} each ship `mineableScatterCommonality
     0.25` / `mineableScatterLumpSizeRange` with no biome gate === vanilla
     GenStep_RocksFromGrid (order 200) reads that field on every rocky player map, same
     universal-leak shape as pyrinth.
  2. The donor's OWN dedicated genstep, `Force_CrystalFormation` (ThingDef_Building/
     CrystalMapGenerator.xml, order 1100, Class Lightsaber.GenStep_ScatterLightsaberCrystals),
     is NOT wired into any MapGeneratorDef's genSteps list today === live def dump query:
     `SELECT def_name FROM defs WHERE def_type='MapGeneratorDef' AND
     json_extract(json,'$.fields.genSteps') LIKE '%Force_CrystalFormation%'` returns 0
     rows (mods=577/6fdca6f582164e2a, captured 2026-09-10T08:36:27Z). So it never fires
     via any known map generator, and needs no PatchOperationRemove today === only the
     universal mineableScatterCommonality leak (point 1) is a live problem.

  Zeroing mineableScatterCommonality here stops the universal vanilla scatter; the
  replacement Deeps-only scatter is RUT_LanternDeepKyberScatter.xml (referenced from
  RUT_LanternDeepGenerator's own genSteps list, which only ever generates a Lantern Deep
  pocket map).

  LIGHTSABER_ABSORB_COPY_DEPLOYED_BESIDE_DONOR (2026-10-26): gated on the DEFS, not on a
  mod. The three formations are defined twice on the live list: by the donor
  lee.theforce.lightsaber (workshop, stays upstream per the owner's 2026-09-02 ruling) and by
  our absorbed copy in mandrake.rsw.armoury (Defs/Absorbed_TheForceLightsaber/, same
  defNames, loads after the donor, so it is the def the game keeps === the 2026-10-26 dump
  attributes all three to mandrake.rsw.armoury). This used to be a PatchOperationFindMod on
  the donor's name: the day the donor leaves the list that gate goes false, the zeroing never
  runs and our copy's 0.25 scatter leaks onto every rocky map, silently. Each Conditional
  below tests the field itself, so it zeroes whichever copies exist (a Replace hits every
  matching node, donor's and ours), and is a quiet no-op when neither does.
  src/RimMandrake/Utils/absorbed_gate_lint.py goes red on a donor-keyed gate over defs we own.
-->
<Patch>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>Defs/ThingDef[defName="Force_CrystalFormation_Small"]/building/mineableScatterCommonality</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationReplace">
      <xpath>Defs/ThingDef[defName="Force_CrystalFormation_Small"]/building/mineableScatterCommonality</xpath>
      <value>
        <mineableScatterCommonality>0</mineableScatterCommonality>
      </value>
    </match>
  </Operation>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>Defs/ThingDef[defName="Force_CrystalFormation_Medium"]/building/mineableScatterCommonality</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationReplace">
      <xpath>Defs/ThingDef[defName="Force_CrystalFormation_Medium"]/building/mineableScatterCommonality</xpath>
      <value>
        <mineableScatterCommonality>0</mineableScatterCommonality>
      </value>
    </match>
  </Operation>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>Defs/ThingDef[defName="Force_CrystalFormation_Large"]/building/mineableScatterCommonality</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationReplace">
      <xpath>Defs/ThingDef[defName="Force_CrystalFormation_Large"]/building/mineableScatterCommonality</xpath>
      <value>
        <mineableScatterCommonality>0</mineableScatterCommonality>
      </value>
    </match>
  </Operation>

  <!-- LANTERNDEEPS_RM_MOD_BUILD_1 (2026-09-25): the kyber scatter GenStepDef
       (RUT_LanternDeepKyberScatter, this file's sibling) moved here with the
       rest of the Star Wars carve-out when RM_LanternDeeps split off as a
       RimMandrake-tier mod, so it is no longer in RM_LanternDeepGenerator's
       own genSteps list. Wire it back in from Utinni — the def itself is
       inert without either copy of the formations (every entry inside it
       carries MayRequireAnyOf="mandrake.rsw.armoury,lee.theforce.lightsaber"),
       so this add is unconditional on either mod,
       only conditional on RM_LanternDeeps existing at all.

       PATCH_MAYREQUIRE_GUARD_INERT_1: the MayRequire this Operation used to
       carry is ignored by vanilla on a top-level <Operation> and was dropped
       rather than fixed — no re-gating needed. The outer <xpath> below IS
       the real guard: it targets RM_LanternDeepGenerator itself, a def
       mandrake.rm.lanterndeeps ("Lantern Deeps") owns, so with that mod
       absent the test matches nothing, no <nomatch> is given, and the
       PatchOperationAdd never runs — a genuine no-op, not a null cross-ref
       injection into always-present content. -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>Defs/MapGeneratorDef[defName="RM_LanternDeepGenerator"]/genSteps</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationAdd">
      <xpath>Defs/MapGeneratorDef[defName="RM_LanternDeepGenerator"]/genSteps</xpath>
      <value>
        <li>RUT_LanternDeepKyberScatter</li>
      </value>
    </match>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
